    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0234" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p1/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751.5 MSP/6–1752: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        France</hi>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d83-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-06-17T18:45:00-04:00">June 17, 1952—6:45
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7404. Pass SRE. Cotel. In course Letourneau talks today,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d83-f2"/> US side informed Fr that subject appropriations US wld be
                    prepared provide <pb facs="0235" n="203" xml:id="pg203"/> up to 150 mil dols
                    addl FY 1953 aid in support overall Fr effort in IC, which probably will remain,
                    as stated in Letourneau memo (Embtel 7682 June 9),<anchor n="3" xml:id="d83-f3"
                    /> substantially same next year. It might be considered this addl aid wld in
                    effect add to Fr resources to meet increased overall Fr requirements in Eur in
                    1953. Relation this addl aid to overall US aid to Fr in FY 1953 and total Fr
                    defense effort in calendar 1953 will be determined in course NATO annual
                    review.</p>
                <p>Fr informed that in view Lisbon understanding, no addl aid available for Fr
                    calendar 1952 budget for IC, but that we are considering Pleven request for add
                    OSP in 1952.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d83-f4"/></p>
                <p>Copies US position paper<anchor n="5" xml:id="d83-f5"/> and minutes being pouched
                    marked Sprouse. Text communiqué fols in separate tel.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d83-f6"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d83-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d83-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Edgar J. Beigel of the Office of Western European Affairs. Repeated
                    for information to London as telegram 6682 and to Saigon as telegram 1984.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f2" n="2" xml:id="d83-f2-content">
                <p>For an extract from the summary minutes, see <ref target="#d82"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f3" n="3" xml:id="d83-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 7682 from Paris, June 9, not printed, contained a summary of a
                    memorandum received from Letourneau at Paris on the same day, which provided
                    information on total French expenditures for Indochina in 1952.
                    (601.5151G/6–952)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f4" n="4" xml:id="d83-f4-content">
                <p>For documentation on overall U.S. assistance to France, see <ref
                        target="frus1952-54v06p1">volume <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >vi</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f5" n="5" xml:id="d83-f5-content">
                <p>Reference is to document LET D–1/1, “Aid Aspects of Letourneau Talks,” June 14,
                    not printed. (Conference files, lot 59 D 95, CF 114)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f6" n="6" xml:id="d83-f6-content">
                <p>Regarding the communiqué of June 18, see editorial note, <ref target="#d84"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">infra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
